Phase 11 -- per-stage timers inside RegistrationVis::computeTransformationImpl.

WHY: RTAB-Map already has excellent timing coverage -- 21 `Timing/*` and 17 `TimingMem/*`
keys in corelib/include/rtabmap/core/Statistics.h:158-197 -- but ALL of it is on the
mapping thread, which runs at Rtabmap/DetectionRate (default 1 Hz).

On the 30 Hz odometry thread you get exactly two numbers:
    OdometryInfo::timeEstimation   (OdometryInfo.h:64, set at Odometry.cpp:819)
    RegistrationInfo::totalTime    (RegistrationInfo.h:79)
Both are whole-frame. There is no breakdown of the stage that consumes 80-90% of it.

This patch adds 8 fields to RegistrationInfo and populates them in RegistrationVis.
Cost: ~16 UTimer::ticks() calls per frame. MEASURED on this machine, gettimeofday is
15.71 ns/call (vDSO works under WSL2), so the added cost is ~0.0003 ms/frame.

--- a/corelib/include/rtabmap/core/RegistrationInfo.h
+++ b/corelib/include/rtabmap/core/RegistrationInfo.h
@@ (in the ctor initializer list, alongside totalTime(0.0))
+		timeDecimation(0.0f),
+		timeKeypointsFrom(0.0f),
+		timeKeypointsTo(0.0f),
+		timeDescriptors(0.0f),
+		timeKeypoints3D(0.0f),
+		timeGuessProjection(0.0f),
+		timeMatching(0.0f),
+		timeMotionEstimation(0.0f),
@@ (in copyWithoutData(), alongside output.icpRMS = icpRMS;)
+		output.timeDecimation       = timeDecimation;
+		output.timeKeypointsFrom    = timeKeypointsFrom;
+		output.timeKeypointsTo      = timeKeypointsTo;
+		output.timeDescriptors      = timeDescriptors;
+		output.timeKeypoints3D      = timeKeypoints3D;
+		output.timeGuessProjection  = timeGuessProjection;
+		output.timeMatching         = timeMatching;
+		output.timeMotionEstimation = timeMotionEstimation;
@@ (in the member block, after `double totalTime;`)
+	// Per-stage breakdown of computeTransformationImpl (seconds).
+	// Only RegistrationVis populates these; RegistrationIcp leaves them at 0.
+	float timeDecimation;
+	float timeKeypointsFrom;
+	float timeKeypointsTo;
+	float timeDescriptors;
+	float timeKeypoints3D;
+	float timeGuessProjection;
+	float timeMatching;
+	float timeMotionEstimation;

--- a/corelib/src/RegistrationVis.cpp
+++ b/corelib/src/RegistrationVis.cpp
@@ near the top of computeTransformationImpl (currently begins at :305)
+	UTimer stageTimer;      // reset at each stage boundary via ticks()
@@ around :455  kptsFrom = _detectorFrom->generateKeypoints(...)
+	info.timeKeypointsFrom = stageTimer.ticks();
@@ around :821  kptsTo = _detectorTo->generateKeypoints(...)
+	info.timeKeypointsTo = stageTimer.ticks();
@@ around :863/:888  generateDescriptors(imageFrom/imageTo, ...)
+	info.timeDescriptors += stageTimer.ticks();
@@ around :921/:957  generateKeypoints3D(...)
+	info.timeKeypoints3D += stageTimer.ticks();
@@ around :1038-1081  cv::projectPoints + rtflann::Index::buildIndex
+	info.timeGuessProjection = stageTimer.ticks();
@@ after the matching loop closes (after :1380 / :1500)
+	info.timeMatching = stageTimer.ticks();
@@ around :1741/:1777/:1839  util3d::estimateMotion3DTo2D / estimateMotion3DTo3D
+	info.timeMotionEstimation = stageTimer.ticks();

OPTIONAL -- surface them over ROS so you can `ros2 topic echo` them:

--- a/rtabmap_msgs/msg/OdomInfo.msg
+++ b/rtabmap_msgs/msg/OdomInfo.msg
@@ after `float32 time_particle_filtering`
+float32 time_keypoints_from
+float32 time_keypoints_to
+float32 time_descriptors
+float32 time_keypoints_3d
+float32 time_guess_projection
+float32 time_matching
+float32 time_motion_estimation

and mirror them in rtabmap_conversions::odomInfoToROS
(rtabmap_conversions/src/MsgConversion.cpp:1760-1839) in the CHEAP section, i.e. BEFORE
the `if(!ignoreData)` block at :1823 -- so they are present on /odom_info_lite and you
never have to subscribe to the expensive full /odom_info to read timings.

NOTE ON MESSAGE COMPATIBILITY: adding fields to OdomInfo.msg changes the message hash.
Every node in the graph must be rebuilt together. If that is unacceptable, skip the .msg
part and read the fields from the RegistrationInfo inside the process instead, or dump
them with ULogger at UINFO level.
